# /etc/inittab for the ticket-204 SD root.
# BusyBox runs action classes in fixed order. Start the DockChannel getty from
# the first sysinit action so it remains available if a later OpenRC job hangs.
::sysinit:/usr/local/sbin/t6040-sdroot-early-console
::sysinit:/usr/local/sbin/t6040-sdroot-openrc sysinit
::sysinit:/usr/local/sbin/t6040-sdroot-openrc boot
::once:/usr/local/sbin/t6040-sdroot-openrc default
::once:/usr/local/sbin/t6040-sdroot-openrc net
# Graphical session. This MUST be here: because /init now refreshes /etc/inittab
# unconditionally, anything the card had but this file lacks is destroyed. That
# is exactly how the GUI was lost on 2026-08-04 -- the card's own inittab carried
# this entry and ours did not, so Xorg and i3 simply stopped being started.
# Rule: this file must be a SUPERSET of whatever the card is expected to run.
::once:/usr/local/sbin/t6040-startx
tty1::respawn:/bin/busybox sh -l
# Direct, dependency-free serial shell. t6040-sdroot-early-console above is the
# nicer path (it runs a real getty with autologin) but it needs
# t6040-b0-ttydc0-console, which needs getty and an autologin helper -- any of
# which being absent silently costs ALL remote access. That happened on
# 2026-08-04: refreshing this inittab replaced a working ttydc0 entry with the
# early-console indirection whose dependency the card did not have. busybox is
# guaranteed present here, so this line cannot fail for a missing dependency.
ttydc0::respawn:/bin/busybox sh -l
::ctrlaltdel:/usr/local/sbin/t6040-sdroot-powerctl reboot
::shutdown:/usr/local/sbin/t6040-sdroot-openrc shutdown
::restart:/run/initramfs/shutdown
